Spec: Holiday entity

Purpose:
  The Holiday entity: a date and a title. A view-less, route-less package used by ../realizations/realizations.sdd,
  ../semester/semester.sdd, ../day_dialog/day_dialog.sdd and ../mcp_server/mcp_server.sdd.

Owns:
  ./domain.py
  ./ports.py
  ./services.py
  ./repository_sqlite.py

References:
  ../architecture.sdd

Depends on:
  ../shared/shared.sdd
  `holidays`, an explicit `pyproject.toml` dependency, for Finnish public holidays

Must:
  A Holiday has a date and a title. Its date is indexed for range listings.
  A date carries at most one Holiday: @HolidayService.add_holiday rejects a date that already holds one with
    @DuplicateHolidayError, @HolidayService.update_holiday re-checks it while ignoring the Holiday being edited,
    and a unique index on the table's date enforces it for a write that bypasses the service. A titled day row
    therefore never depends on which Holiday the view happens to read last.
  A Holiday has no foreign key: holidays are global to the calendar, not owned by a Semester or a Course.
  @HolidayService.add_holiday rejects an empty title with @InvalidHolidayError before storage.
  @HolidayService.update_holiday applies the same title check as @HolidayService.add_holiday and rejects an
  unknown id with @UnknownHolidayError.
  @HolidayService.delete_holiday removes one Holiday, rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownHolidayError.
  @HolidayService.create_defaults_for_range stores every Finnish public holiday whose date falls in the given range
    and skips a date that already holds a Holiday, so it is safe to call for a range that is partly populated. It
    asks for Finnish names explicitly rather than letting the host's locale decide them, so the stored titles do not
    depend on the environment, and it covers only the range it is given rather than whole calendar years.
  @HolidayRepository in ./ports.py exposes operations to get, list holidays for a date range, and to add, update
    and delete one.
  The table is created automatically on startup when it does not exist, and its unique date index replaces an
    earlier non-unique index of the same name instead of leaving the constraint absent.

Tasks:
  [x] Decide that a Holiday may be edited and deleted after creation
  [x] Add @HolidayService.get_holiday, @HolidayService.update_holiday and @HolidayService.delete_holiday with the
    matching @HolidayRepository operations, rejecting an unknown id with @UnknownHolidayError
  [x] Implement @Holiday in ./domain.py and a hardcoded ./services.py returning one placeholder Holiday within the
    hardcoded Semester's date range, standing in for @HolidayRepository until persistence exists
  [x] Replace the hardcoded ./services.py with a class-based @HolidayRepository-backed `HolidayService`
    (./ports.py and ./repository_sqlite.py), per ../architecture.sdd's Example
  [x] Reject empty Holiday titles in @HolidayService.add_holiday with @InvalidHolidayError
  [x] Keep at most one Holiday per date: reject a duplicate date in @HolidayService.add_holiday and
    @HolidayService.update_holiday with @DuplicateHolidayError, back it with a unique index on the date, and
    replace an earlier non-unique index of the same name
  [x] Add @HolidayService.create_defaults_for_range, backed by the `holidays` package, that stores a range's Finnish
    public holidays and skips dates that already hold one
